      "translation": {
        "english_text": "(Kumaran's mother comes carrying a water pot. Kumaran, kurukkodi—has been chopping firewood, sweating. Exhausted, he sits down—idli arrives—he delights. Next an orange arrives—he is comforted. Milk comes for the labourer Kumaran—he is enraptured. In this way, through things carrying the flavour of love, Meenu conveyed her feelings to Kumaran. Finally, the two together lifted that beautiful flower-pot, their faces blossoming into smiles.)",
        "mode": "prose-faithful",
        "notes": [
          "The verified source form `குறுக்கொடிய` is not silently repaired; it is retained as `kurukkodi` within the English stage-direction unit."
        ]
      }
